The conjugate method is used to simplify complex fractions. We multiply the numerator and denominator of each fraction by the conjugate of the denominator. This eliminates the imaginary part from the denominator. \[
\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \cdot \frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} + \frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \cdot \frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i}
\] \[
= \frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)} + \frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}
\] \[
= \frac{(9 - 25) + (30i)}{9 + 25} + \frac{(9 - 25) - (30i)}{9 + 25}
\] \[
= \frac{-16 + 30i}{34} + \frac{-16 - 30i}{34}
\] \[
= \frac{-32}{34}
\] \[
= \frac{-16}{17}
